🚀 Task 9 - Deploy Strapi using ECS Fargate Spot (No CloudWatch)
📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates deploying a Strapi CMS application on Amazon ECS using Fargate Spot, with infrastructure fully managed using Terraform.

The deployment intentionally excludes CloudWatch monitoring as per task requirement.

This setup showcases containerized deployment, infrastructure as code (IaC), IAM configuration, networking setup, and cost optimization using Fargate Spot.

🏗️ Architecture Overview

The infrastructure includes:

Amazon ECS Cluster

ECS Task Definition

ECS Service

Fargate Spot Capacity Provider

IAM Execution Role

Security Group

Default VPC & Subnets

Public IP Assignment

Docker Image stored in Amazon ECR

🛠️ Technologies Used

Amazon Web Services (AWS)

Amazon ECS

AWS Fargate Spot

AWS IAM

AWS VPC

Amazon ECR

Terraform

Docker

Git & GitHub

📂 Project Structure
TASK-9-Deploy-Strapi-using-ECS-Fargate-Spot-No-CloudWatch/
└── strapi-fargate-spot/
    ├── main.tf
    ├── iam.tf
    ├── provider.tf
    ├── outputs.tf
    ├── .terraform.lock.hcl
    ├── .gitignore
    ├── README.md
    └── my-strapi/
⚙️ Infrastructure Details
1️⃣ AWS Provider

Defines AWS region and provider configuration.

2️⃣ Networking

Uses Default VPC

Dynamically fetches default subnets

3️⃣ Security Group

Allows inbound traffic on port 1337

Allows all outbound traffic

4️⃣ ECS Cluster

Creates a dedicated ECS cluster:

izan-strapi-cluster-v2
5️⃣ ECS Task Definition

Launch Type Compatibility: FARGATE

CPU: 512

Memory: 1024

Container Port: 1337

Docker Image: Pulled from Amazon ECR

IAM Execution Role attached

6️⃣ ECS Service

Desired Count: 1

Capacity Provider: FARGATE_SPOT

Assign Public IP: Enabled

Custom Security Group Attached

🚀 Deployment Steps
1️⃣ Initialize Terraform
terraform init
2️⃣ Plan Infrastructure
terraform plan
3️⃣ Apply Configuration
terraform apply

Terraform will create:

ECS Cluster

Security Group

IAM Role

Task Definition

ECS Service

🌍 Accessing the Application

After successful deployment:

Go to AWS Console

Navigate to ECS → Cluster → Service → Tasks

Click running task

Copy Public IP

Open in browser:

http://PUBLIC-IP:1337

If everything is configured correctly, Strapi CMS will load successfully.

🔐 Security & Best Practices

.env file is excluded from repository

.terraform folder is ignored

Terraform state files are not committed

IAM role limited to ECS execution permissions

No hardcoded credentials in repository

💡 Key Learnings

Deploying containerized applications using ECS Fargate

Using Fargate Spot for cost optimization

Managing infrastructure with Terraform

IAM role configuration for ECS tasks

Handling launch type vs capacity provider conflicts

Cleaning Git repository (removing large files and secrets)

Debugging ECS service deployment errors

💰 Cost Optimization

Using FARGATE_SPOT significantly reduces compute costs compared to standard Fargate.

This approach is ideal for non-production or interruptible workloads.
